SteamOS has no COLLADA DOM, so the OpenSceneGraph fork that OpenMW fetches for static builds never creates
its .dae plugin target. OpenMW always lists osgdb_dae among the statically linked plugins, so configuring
fails with 'Target "osgdb_dae" not found'. Drop the plugin when COLLADA DOM is missing: only some mods use
.dae models (vanilla Morrowind is all NIF), and OpenMW's runtime plugin check is skipped for static OSG.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
index c52d380..f9792fb 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -320,6 +320,9 @@ if(NOT COLLADA_DOM_VERSION_MINOR)
 endif()
 
 find_package(collada_dom 2.5)
+if(NOT collada_dom_FOUND)
+    list(REMOVE_ITEM USED_OSG_PLUGINS osgdb_dae)
+endif()
 
 option(OPENMW_USE_SYSTEM_ICU "Use system ICU library instead of internal. If disabled, requires autotools" ON)
 if(OPENMW_USE_SYSTEM_ICU)
